# Owners of the paths that decide how code is built, checked, deployed and rolled back.
#
# Informational for now: with a single maintainer, "Require review from Code Owners"
# must stay OFF in the `main` and `staging` rulesets. GitHub never lets the author of a
# PR approve it, so with that option on, every PR touching these paths (including the
# owner's own) could never be merged. Turn it on once there is a second reviewer.
# Later lines win over earlier ones; paths are relative to the repository root.

